{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 46,
  "title": "Travelling",
  "description": "Name the things of a journey, and say where you are going.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Travel words are the ones a learner needs on the first day abroad, and they are ordinary nouns with an article and a plural.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El pasaporte, el vuelo, el equipaje, el hotel y el conductor are masculine. La maleta, la aduana, la frontera y la reserva are feminine. El equipaje is the whole of it, and la maleta is one case. El conductor is the driver, and el andén is the platform at the station.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el pasaporte",
            "en": "the passport"
          },
          {
            "es": "la maleta",
            "en": "the suitcase"
          },
          {
            "es": "el andén",
            "en": "the platform"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where you are going",
        "body": "You already know how to say where a place is and how to get there. Ir + a + place says where you are going: voy al hotel, voy a la aduana. En la frontera means at the border, and la reserva is the booking you made before you left.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "voy al hotel",
            "en": "I am going to the hotel"
          },
          {
            "es": "la maleta está en el equipaje",
            "en": "the suitcase is in the luggage"
          },
          {
            "es": "hago la reserva para noviembre",
            "en": "I make the booking for November"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
